{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/61952-court-positions","id":61952,"title":"Court Positions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-30T20:13:09-08:00","id":61952,"title":"Court Positions","content":"What are some of the basic court positions that tend to show up in Changeling (aside from the monarch) as well as some more permanent positions that don't change with the seasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T20:17:48-08:00","id":61955,"title":"","content":"There's a writeup for each court in Lords of Summer. Basically, most courts will have a person to serve as envoy to the other courts and one to serve as a martial leader (or whatever passes for one). Beyond that, it depends on the court in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T20:19:19-08:00","id":61959,"title":"","content":"Quite a few Entitlements probably qualify as well. The Viziers positively leap to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T20:32:11-08:00","id":61961,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you. I completely forgot that LoS discussed the courts. What's an Entitlement? (decently new to changeling, I've heard the term before I just forget its meaning)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T20:56:51-08:00","id":61974,"title":"","content":"Entitlements are the Changeling nobility, more or less (some are way, way more glamorous than others). Each Entitlement is basically an order of like-minded Changelings. Being a part of an Entitlement grants 1-3 privileges, which are usually fairly minor special powers (much more powerful in the case of the Eldritch Orders).<br /> <br /> For example, the Viziers I mentioned can be found in Equinox Road. They're extremely powerful Changeling Sorcerers that join the order to prevent their Clarity from slipping further than it already has. They swear to put the needs of the Freehold ahead of their own and serve the current ruler to the best of their ability. In return they become immortal (although their age catches up to them should they ever leave the Entitlement), get cheaper Contracts (so long as they can justify them to help the Vizier help the Freehold), and gain some resistance from gaining new Derangements and having current ones activate.<br /> <br /> Some Entitlements will likely have rather formal positions in the Courts as a consequence. Others though, like the Pilgrims of the Endless Road (a group of Changelings dedicated to self-improvement, basically) don't really have any official function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T21:25:01-08:00","id":61983,"title":"","content":"I see, I see. I will definitely look them up. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T16:41:52-08:00","id":62563,"title":"","content":"To compare Changeling to other games, Entitlements are similar to Bloodlines, Lodges, or Legacies - a way to further develop your character, if you choose. Not all of them officially interact with the Freehold and not all Freeholds will have someone from a given Entitlement, so it's less that the Entitlements play roles in the Freehold than that certain roles in a Freehold are commonly held by members of certain Entitlements. <br /> <br /> You might want to look to traditional feudal court organization for ideas for court positions. Your freehold might have a Steward who takes the Monarch's orders and plots out how to get them done (and who may or may not actually be trustworthy). Perhaps there's a set of Rangers and Boundsmen who patrol the Hedge for danger (and who need a Captain), and quite possibly a Guard who do the same thing for the mortal side of things. If the Freehold has an official meeting-place such as a joint Hollow or a building in the Real, they might have a Seneschal or keeper-of-the-keys dedicated to the care of the place. If there are other Freeholds nearby there might be ambassadors or emissaries to or from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:10:56-08:00","id":65852,"title":"","content":"I have a list of secondary freehold positions at the bottom of my<b> <a href=\"http://www.vtm.kismetrose.com/ctl/ChangelingFreeholds.html\" target=\"_blank\">freehold worksheet</a></b>; they were culled from across books like Lords of Summer and my gaming experiences. I hope they help. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name"